# estimator — the CLI's source is committed; all its runtime data lives in the
# sibling estimator-data/ directory (DATA_ROOT in estimator/src/db.ts, default
# resolve(ROOT, "..", "estimator-data"), overridable via EST_DATA_ROOT) and is
# never committed (design R3 §4, §10 Q11): estimator.db (+ -wal/-shm sidecars),
# sweep.lock, spool/, backups/, board.html and board.md all land there — one
# directory to ignore instead of one entry per artifact, and `git clean` in the
# checkout can never touch the corpus.
estimator-data/
# gate probes: the .ts scanners are code and committed; everything they PRODUCE is
# corpus-derived data and stays local — this repo is public (decision 11: no
# estimate/actual/spend data, no prompt or conversation content, ever)
estimator/gates/*.json
estimator/gates/*.md
# the spec and decision log quote private prompts and real usage data — local only,
# covered by the weekly backups/ snapshot, not by git
estimator/DESIGN.md
estimator/DECISIONS.md
# design docs (e.g. HOOK-BINDING-SPEC.md) are drafted alongside DESIGN.md/DECISIONS.md
# and carry the same private-corpus caveats even when they avoid quoting numbers
# directly — local only, not part of the committed source (HOOK-BINDING-SPEC.md §10 step 0)
estimator/design/
# `bun install` materialises the two typecheck-only devDependencies here. Runtime
# dependencies are still zero; `bun.lock` IS committed, so `bun run typecheck`
# reproduces exactly the compiler the last recorded run used.
estimator/node_modules/
daemon-auth-cooldown
daemon-auth-status.json
# Server-managed settings caches written by the harness
policy-limits.json
policy-limits.json.signature*.json
remote-settings.json
remote-settings.json.signature*.json
remote-settings-consent.json
